{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "משגה עור", :translit "mashgeh ivver", :gloss "misleading a blind man"} {:he "לא תיעץ לו לפי דרכך", :translit "lo ta'itz lo lefi darkha", :gloss "do not advise him according to your way"} {:he "כדי להסיג גבולו", :translit "kedei lehasig g'vulo", :gloss "in order to move his boundary"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Applies the prohibition to a concrete case: giving self-serving advice to trap someone into violating a boundary"}], :frame {:text "The rabbis derive that 'a blind man' in Deuteronomy 27:18 is not only one who cannot see but anyone lacking knowledge in a given matter (Sifrei Deuteronomy 282). The same prohibition is applied to giving misleading advice, especially where the adviser has a hidden financial stake — the paradigm case being one who counsels another to move a boundary to the adviser's advantage. Moving a boundary is itself independently prohibited in Deuteronomy 19:14, 'You shall not move your fellow's boundary-marker.'", :sources ["Sifrei Deuteronomy 282" "Deuteronomy 19:14"]}} {:quotes [{:he "משגה", :translit "mashgeh", :gloss "misleading"} {:he "ב'", :translit "bet", :gloss "two"} {:he "משגה עור", :translit "mashgeh ivver", :gloss "misleading a blind man"} {:he "משגה ישרים בדרך רע", :translit "mashgeh y'sharim ba-derekh ra", :gloss "misleading the upright on an evil way"} {:he "שררשו משגה עור", :translit "she-rishro mashgeh ivver", :gloss "whose root is misleading a blind man"} {:he "שמיעצו לחטוא", :translit "she-ma'itz'o lachto", :gloss "who advises him to sin"} {:he "שהוא ישר", :translit "she-hu yashar", :gloss "who is upright"} {:he "ונותן לו עצה לעקם דרכיו", :translit "u-noten lo etzah la'akem dar'khav", :gloss "and gives him counsel to pervert his ways"} {:he "וסמך לו", :translit "u-samach lo", :gloss "and it is juxtaposed to it"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["משגה עור" "משגה ישרים בדרך רע"]}], :frame {:text "Isaiah 3:12 reads 'משגה ישרים בדרך רע, My people — its exactors mislead the upright on an evil way.' The phrase describes leaders who themselves walk uprightly yet steer others toward crookedness, which Ba'al HaTurim contrasts with 'משגה עור' of Deuteronomy 27:18. The principle of deriving legal or conceptual teachings from the juxtaposition (סמיכות) of adjacent verses is a recognized rabbinic method, employed throughout Talmudic and midrashic literature.", :sources ["Isaiah 3:12"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Applies the prohibition to a concrete case: giving self-serving advice to trap someone into violating a boundary", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["משגה עור" "משגה ישרים בדרך רע"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "משגה עור", :refs ["Deuteronomy 27:18"], :n 1, :lens :exact} {:phrase "משגה ישרים בדרך רע", :refs ["Proverbs 28:10"], :n 1, :lens :exact}]}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:39:54.694429880Z", :model "glm-5.2"}